.TH tupatch n 0.3 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tupatch
.PP
Apply unified diffs in pure Tcl. This module is the counterpart to \fBtclutils::tudiff\fR.
.SS Package
.CS
package require tclutils::tupatch 0.3
.CE
.SS API
.CS
::tclutils::tupatch::parse patchText
::tclutils::tupatch::text sourceText patchText ?-reverse 0|1? ?-strict 0|1?
::tclutils::tupatch::fromFile sourceFile patchText ?-reverse 0|1? ?-strict 0|1?
.CE
.SS Options
.IP \(bu
\fB\-reverse 0|1\fR: apply the patch backwards. Default: \fB0\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fB\-strict 0|1\fR: verify context and delete lines against the source. Default: \fB1\fR.
.PP
Both take any Tcl boolean (\fB0\fR/\fB1\fR, \fByes\fR/\fBno\fR, \fBtrue\fR/\fBfalse\fR, \fBon\fR/\fBoff\fR); anything else raises \fB{TCLUTILS COMMON BOOLEAN \-reverse}\fR or \fB\-strict\fR.
.SS Example
.CS
package require tclutils::tudiff
package require tclutils::tupatch

set old "alpha\nbeta\n"
set new "alpha\nBETA\n"

set patch  [::tclutils::tudiff::unifiedText $old $new]
set result [::tclutils::tupatch::text $old $patch]
.CE
.SS "Error codes"
.IP \(bu
\fB{TCLUTILS TUPATCH CONTEXT}\fR: context/delete line does not match the source.
.IP \(bu
\fB{TCLUTILS TUPATCH RANGE}\fR: hunk position is outside the source or overlaps an earlier hunk.
.IP \(bu
\fB{TCLUTILS COMMON OPTION ...}\fR: invalid option from \fBcommon::parseOptions\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fB{TCLUTILS COMMON BOOLEAN \-reverse}\fR, \fB{TCLUTILS COMMON BOOLEAN \-strict}\fR: the option value is not a boolean.
.SS Notes
.PP
\fBtupatch\fR uses the same line model as \fBtudiff\fR: lines are split and re\-joined with \fB\en\fR. The line end at the end of the text is kept: a source ending with \fB\en\fR gives a result ending with \fB\en\fR. The marker \fB\e\e No newline at end of file\fR works as in \fBdiff \-u\fR: after a \fB+\fR line the result ends without \fB\en\fR, after a \fB\-\fR line (and none after \fB+\fR) it gets one; \fB\-reverse\fR swaps both. \fBparse\fR reports the markers as \fBoldNoNl\fR and \fBnewNoNl\fR in each hunk (0.3; 0.2 always dropped the final \fB\en\fR).
